@ [exploded] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Public_Procedure_Schema_Direction_Profile.exploded.sop

& [Directions] are closed and explicit
  + input_deserialize describes bytes accepted through strict decode
  + output_serialize describes values emitted through strict encode
  + every schema document, definition universe, definition account, fingerprint, residual, and compatibility result carries exactly one direction

& [Identity] is two-level
  + semantic type identity remains independent of transport direction
  + contract definition identity is the pair direction and stable type name
  + one semantic type may have identities in both directions
  + PreparedRunRequest has an output_serialize identity when preparation emits it and an input_deserialize identity when run accepts it

& [DefinitionUniverses] are isolated
  + input_definitions is generated only under the schemars Deserialize contract
  + output_definitions is generated only under the schemars Serialize contract
  + each universe is a closed local-reference graph with its own deterministic lexical traversal and counters
  + local references resolve only within the document and direction that emitted them
  + no cache entry, definition, or reference crosses direction

& [DocumentAssignments] are exact
  + prepare_input, run_input, and verify_input use input_deserialize
  + base_response and preparation_response use output_serialize
  + every later root must declare its direction before generation
  + a mixed or absent direction is a typed formation fault

& [Fingerprints] preserve both structure and contract
  + raw_content_digest is SHA-256 of normalized definition bytes and may demonstrate current structural equality
  + contract_fingerprint is SHA-256 over profile id, zero separator, direction, zero separator, stable type name, zero separator, and normalized bytes
  + equal bytes across directions do not produce equal contract fingerprints
  + bundle and document fingerprints bind the direction-bearing ordered contents

& [Compatibility] compares like with like
  + input compatibility compares only input_deserialize baselines
  + output compatibility compares only output_serialize baselines
  + cross-direction raw equality is informational and grants no substitution authority
  + a direction change is a contract identity change even when raw bytes are unchanged

& [Conformance] binds behavior without replacing it
  + input instances are checked against strict deserialization behavior and input schemas
  + output fixtures are produced by actual serialization and checked against output schemas
  + PreparedRunRequest receives independent fixtures and fingerprints in both directions
  + strict serde, recursive closure, core semantic bounds, residuals, and authority admission remain independent gates

& [Failures] are fail closed
  + absent, unknown, or mixed direction
  + opposite-contract cache reuse
  + cross-universe local-reference resolution
  + incomplete two-direction account for a crossing type
  + fingerprint preimage ambiguity or normalization instability
  + same-direction golden change without compatibility classification

& [ImplementationSequence] is narrow
  + CSD-I01 add optional exact schema capability and direction-aware derive inventory under a separately signed CPMS-I02 activation
  + CSD-I02 generate two isolated definition universes, accounts, normalization, and domain-separated fingerprints
  + CSD-I03 add directional root documents, crossing-type fixtures, goldens, and compatibility reports
  + each step requires focused review before the next

& [AuthorityBoundary] is formation only
  + this specification resolves contract direction but does not activate implementation
  - never: add a dependency, derive or generate a schema, alter public transport, register a provider, call a model, use a service, persist, network, effect, or implement hardware

& [SignatureCandidate] is formed not activated
  + [candidate_signature_uuid] is a96e0541-810c-4fc2-a64d-0abaf5d9bea1
  + [activation_condition] is exact canonical hash, direct dependency pin, 87-type source-touch review, optional-feature design, and separate CPMS-I02 claim

